<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Fortified Features Framework + EPOE-Forked: EPOE's muscle stimulator (arms; +50 carrying capacity) qualifies a pawn for
		the heavy weapons of the three lightest Fortified tiers (AverageHumanCanUse 1.0, LightAutomatroid 1.1,
		StandardAutomatroid 1.4 body size).
		This is an XML approximation of "DMS-EPOE More Compatibility Patch" (sunsalfriedrice.DMS.EPOE.More.CompatPatch,
		workshop 3781470754). That mod's DLL requires the full set together: 10 bionic fingers, 2 muscle stimulators,
		2 optimized shoulders and 2 optimized hands. Fortified's whitelist can only say "any one of these hediffs", so a
		combination cannot be expressed in XML; the muscle stimulator, EPOE's strength implant, stands in for the set. It is
		looser than the original: one stimulator is enough.
		The DLL is not taken over: its CanEquip postfix also sets "cannot equip" for every pawn without the full set, even
		pawns that already qualify by body size, gene, apparel or another whitelisted hediff.
		Kept apart from FortifiedEPOE so it still loads when DMS-EPOE Compatibility Patch 1.6 is active.
		Verified 2026-10-21: MuscleStimulatorArms exists in EPOE-Forked 1.6.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
				<xpath>Defs/Fortified.HeavyEquippableDef[(defName="AverageHumanCanUse" or defName="LightAutomatroid" or defName="StandardAutomatroid") and not(EquippableWithHediff)]</xpath>
				<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/Fortified.HeavyEquippableDef[(defName="AverageHumanCanUse" or defName="LightAutomatroid" or defName="StandardAutomatroid") and not(EquippableWithHediff)]</xpath>
					<value>
						<EquippableWithHediff />
					</value>
				</match>
			</li>
			<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/Fortified.HeavyEquippableDef[defName="AverageHumanCanUse" or defName="LightAutomatroid" or defName="StandardAutomatroid"]/EquippableWithHediff</xpath>
				<value>
					<li>MuscleStimulatorArms</li>
				</value>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
